  "reason": "Evidence: config_024 (multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) achieved 0.629 acc, a ~9.3% jump over the best singleprofile multimodal (config_022: 0.535), confirming multiprofile is the dominant design lever. The aggregation method (avgpool) is the one untested dimension within this best-performing family. Question: Does transformer-based aggregation of multiple profiles capture inter-profile structure that simple averaging misses, yielding further gains over 0.629? Why this experiment: config_026 is a clean single-variable extension of the current best (only aggregation changes from avgpool to transformer), giving a direct A/B comparison. If it improves, we identify a better aggregation strategy to build on; if it does not, we confirm avgpool is sufficient and can redirect budget toward RNA encoder or fusion-method variations. Under a tight budget, this maximizes information per experiment by isolating one hypothesis on the most promising configuration."
}

